Chronicle Draw Steel — licensing
================================

This package contains two different kinds of material with two different
licensing positions. They are stated separately on purpose: flattening them
into a single claim is what this file used to do, and it was wrong.


1. DRAW STEEL rules text (most of data/)
----------------------------------------

The rules text reproduced in data/ — glossary terms, skills, ancestries, kits,
abilities, ability keywords, the ancestry point-buy budget, the monster-making
and encounter-building formulas, and the animal traits — is DRAW STEEL game
content. It is reproduced under MCDM Productions' DRAW STEEL Creator License.
It is NOT Creative Commons material: MCDM has not released Draw Steel under any
Creative Commons licence, and there is no Draw Steel SRD or free basic-rules
tier.

    This package is an independent product published under the DRAW STEEL
    Creator License and is not affiliated with MCDM Productions, LLC.
    DRAW STEEL © 2024 MCDM Productions, LLC.

No MCDM trademarks, logos, art, or proprietary setting material are reproduced
here — only rules text and its mechanical numbers. MCDM endorsement is not
implied.

This package does not, and cannot, sublicense that rules text. Anyone
redistributing it is relying on the same Creator License and must carry the
same attribution. data/NOTICE.md records, file by file, exactly what is
reproduced, from where, and what was deliberately left out.


2. This package's own work (everything else)
--------------------------------------------

Everything this package's contributors wrote themselves is licensed
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0):

  - widgets/*.js   — the widget source code
  - tools/*.mjs    — the build and test tooling
  - docs/*         — the design, schema, and handoff documentation
  - manifest.json  — the package manifest and its schema declarations
  - the data entries flagged "source": "custom", and the specific fields
    named in an entry's properties.custom_fields

  Copyright (c) the Chronicle Draw Steel contributors.
  Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

CC-BY-4.0 is the licence this package has always declared; what changed is its
scope. It covers the contributors' own work only. It never covered, and could
not have covered, MCDM's rules text.

(CC-BY-4.0 is an unusual choice for source code — Creative Commons itself
recommends a software licence for software. Section 2 preserves the choice this
project already made rather than substituting a new one; whether to move
widgets/ and tools/ to a software licence such as MIT or Apache-2.0 is a
decision for the maintainers, not a correction.)


A limitation, stated rather than papered over
---------------------------------------------

The text of the DRAW STEEL Creator License itself could not be read while this
file was written: mcdmproductions.com is unreachable from the environment this
work was done in, and repeated attempts by separate authors hit the same wall.
Every statement above about what the Creator License permits rests on the
position already established in this repository and on the community Steel
Compendium's published reliance on the same licence for the same material — not
on a reading of the licence text.

A human should read

    https://www.mcdmproductions.com/draw-steel-creator-license

once and confirm this position, specifically: that the licence permits
reproducing rules text in a free, open-source product; that the attribution
wording quoted in section 1 is the wording it requires; and that offering this
package's own original work under CC-BY-4.0 alongside it is compatible with its
terms.

Until that has happened, treat sections 1 and 2 as this project's good-faith
statement of its position, not as legal advice.
